                                "sense_id": "4db078ee-3ab4-3e8a-8b90-b5a2af3bc000",
                                "text": "“Bill was born near Des Moines, Iowa, and as a boy was knowed as the champion lightweight corn shucker of Hog Bristle County. […]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d81bd343-e715-4566-bc14-3bcf36771a4e",
                                "sense_id": "4db078ee-3ab4-3e8a-8b90-b5a2af3bc000",
                                "text": "Everyone drank gimlets and the hostess hired an oyster shucker to come up from Baltimore with crates and crates of oysters."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e9b680a-bc71-3a20-8f8b-02ddabea838a",
                        "entry_id": "e838452d-c6d1-3173-84e9-47a230dab6f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who shucks or removes something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
